.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- generated, not tracked -------------------------------------------------
#
# The synthetic training set is 63,000 files / 73 MB and regenerates in about
# two minutes, deterministically from the seed in dataset_meta.json. Cloning it
# would be slower than rebuilding it, and git keeps every byte forever even if
# it is deleted later. `python -m micr.build` recreates it byte for byte.
#
# What IS tracked is the font it is rendered from: 3.7 KB that expands into the
# whole dataset. That is the training data, in its compressed form.
dataset/
debug/

# --- model artefacts, tracked -----------------------------------------------
#
# The training box is headless, so pushing the finished model back to the repo
# is how it gets collected. Half a megabyte each.
!models/
!models/*.pth
!models/*_training_report.json
!models/*_test_real.json
!export/
!export/*.tflite
!export/*.onnx
!export/micr_labels.json
!export/micr_labels.txt

# ... but not the onnx2tf scratch directory.
export/_onnx2tf_*/

# --- real check data, never tracked -----------------------------------------
#
# The photos carry customer names, addresses and signatures. labels.txt carries
# the MICR lines, and the cut crops encode glyph position in their filenames, so
# the full line reassembles from a folder listing. A routing number plus an
# account number is everything needed to originate an ACH debit against that
# account, so none of it belongs in a repo -- least of all a public one.
#
# Real checks are NOT needed to train: the model learns from glyphs rendered
# from the font. They only add a test_real accuracy number.
#
# Back labels.txt up somewhere private. It is the one hand-written artefact,
# and regenerating the crops depends on it.
checks/*
!checks/labels.example.txt

# --- fonts ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Excluded by default, since a commercial E-13B licence usually forbids
# redistribution. The OFL build is the exception: SIL OFL 1.1 explicitly allows
# bundling and redistribution, so it and its licence are tracked.
fonts/*
!fonts/README.md
!fonts/E13B-OFL.ttf
!fonts/E13B-OFL.LICENSE.md
!fonts/E13B-OFL.UPSTREAM-README.md
!fonts/E13B-OFL.svgs/
